graph-const-error = The constant expression produces an error.
graph-declaration-type = Declaration type is invalid or unavailable.
graph-type-declaration = The declared type is not valid.
graph-analysis-limit = Graph analysis exceeds the host's admission limits.
graph-analysis-cancelled = Graph analysis was cancelled.
graph-domain-unsupported = This execution domain is unavailable.
graph-domain-analysis-blocked = Graph analysis requires supported execution domains.
graph-metadata-stale = Node metadata no longer matches this document.
graph-port-unknown = Connection references an unknown port.
graph-port-direction = Connection must run from an output port to an input port.
graph-kind-mismatch = Connection ports have incompatible kinds.
graph-fanin-data = Data input has more than one connection.
graph-fanout-exec = Execution output has more than one connection.
graph-fanout-event = Event output has more than one connection.
graph-stream-fanout = Stream output has more than one consumer.
graph-scope-edge = Connection crosses graph body scopes.
graph-type-mismatch = Connection port types are incompatible.
graph-signature-missing = Node has no stored signature snapshot.
graph-provider-missing = Node has no provider binding.
graph-package-lock-missing = Node provider package version is not locked.
graph-provider-unavailable = Node definition or exact provider is unavailable.
graph-dependency-unavailable = Node cannot be checked because a connected node is unresolved.
graph-intrinsic-unsupported = This core version does not support this language intrinsic yet.
graph-signature-drift = Stored node signature differs from the resolved definition.
graph-type-ambiguous = A generic node has unresolved type parameters.
graph-type-complexity = Type analysis exceeded its resource limit.
graph-constraint-unsatisfied = A type argument does not satisfy its constraint.
graph-no-specialization = Provider does not support the resolved type arguments.
graph-input-required = Required input has no value.
graph-variadic-identity = Variadic counters are duplicated or inconsistent with the next counter.
graph-type-codec = A saved type codec is unavailable in the resolved registry.
graph-variadic-count = The number of variadic port instances is outside the allowed range.
graph-literal-type = Input literal does not match the declared port type.
graph-handle-literal = Handle ports cannot have literals.
graph-literal-shadowed = Input literal is shadowed by a connected edge.
graph-suspends-missing = Suspension metadata is required for this node kind.
graph-suspends-invalid = Suspension metadata conflicts with the node kind.
graph-recursion = Function calls contain a recursion cycle.
graph-function-kind = Declared function kind differs from the inferred body kind.
graph-call-target-missing = Function call requires a canonical function target.
graph-call-target-unknown = Function call target is not declared in this graph.
graph-function-metadata-unavailable = Function body or leaf semantics are unavailable.
graph-function-interface = Function interface is malformed: ports must be unique typed data ports using declared type parameters.
graph-variable-unknown = Variable reference is missing, invalid or undeclared.
graph-variable-scope = Workspace variables require an asynchronous shared write.
graph-shared-variable-scope = Shared writes require a workspace variable.
graph-cycle-data = Data dependencies contain a cycle.
graph-update-operation = Variable update requires a supported operation.
graph-update-unsupported = This variable update operation is not supported by this core version.
graph-entry-in-function = Entry and watch nodes are not permitted in a function.
graph-subscription-in-function = Subscriptions are not permitted in a function.
graph-event-unknown = Event reference is missing, invalid or undeclared.
graph-connection-unknown = Connection reference is missing, invalid or undeclared.
graph-activation-policy = Entry activation policy is missing or invalid.
graph-converter-config = Converter node uses an unsupported or malformed config.
graph-converter-entry = Converter registry entry is unavailable.
graph-converter-options = Converter options are invalid or incomplete.
graph-function-body-marker = Function entry, return and output markers do not match the declared interface.
graph-missing-return = A path of this function ends without reaching a return.
graph-region-ambiguous = This node is reached from inside a branch, step or loop body and also from outside it. Join after the construct's completed output, or use a copy of the node on each path.
graph-region-escape = An execution connection leaves its region.
graph-unavailable-value = A value is not available on every path that reaches this input.
graph-cross-activation = This value comes from a trigger that may not be the one running here. A chain several triggers share can read only what all of them provide, such as variables.
graph-break-outside-loop = Break and continue need an enclosing loop body in the same function.
graph-cycle-sync-control = A control cycle needs a node that always suspends.
graph-loop-unbounded = A while loop requires a finite positive max_iterations.
graph-zone-structure = A zone needs a matching begin and end, a pure body and no values leaving it except through the end.
graph-switch-case = Switch cases need distinct values of the key's kind; an enum switch covers every variant or connects default.
graph-for-each-mode = For each mode must be list or map.
graph-manual-payload = A manual entry payload must name a concrete registered type, and no other field is allowed.
graph-nominal-config = A record or enum node must name a registered record or enum type and an existing field or variant, and no other field.
graph-timer-config = A timer entry needs a positive interval or a non-negative delay in nanoseconds, and only its documented fields.
graph-watch-config = When needs valid settings for its mode and ordered bounds that fit the watched type.
graph-variable-changed = A variable-changed entry needs a run variable with an initial value and a type with eq.
graph-busy-loop = This control cycle only yields and keeps the CPU busy.
graph-unreachable = Execution node is not reachable from any entry or region root.
graph-write-conflict = Parallel Fork branches write the same variable without a compatible policy.
graph-handle-persist = Handle types cannot be persisted, shared, written as literals or exported.
graph-stream-store = Streams cannot be stored in variables or exported.
graph-stale-capture = A value captured before a suspension is written back; use update-variable.
graph-variable-persistent = Local variables cannot be persistent.
graph-register-config = Register scope must be run or activation and initial must be a literal of its type.
graph-detach-in-function = A return cancels the detached strands left by this fork.
graph-export-target = Export does not name an existing data output port.
graph-export-duplicate = Export identifier is used more than once.
graph-export-type = Exported value type cannot be serialized.
graph-config-invalid = Node configuration does not satisfy its definition schema.
graph-config-schema-unsupported = Definition config schema uses constructs outside the supported dialect.
